    <h1 style="text-align: center; color: #003366;">Predicting improvements in student achievement</h1>
    <h2 style="text-align: center; color: #333;">Achievement outcomes</h2>
    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
        <li>For elementary/middle schools, we use average ITBS gain scores in reading and math based on a CCSR-developed measure of individual student growth from the prior year.</li>
        <li>At the high school level, we do not have value-added scores, so we use average school performance in reading and math in 2002-2003, but include a prior 8th-grade achievement score for entering freshmen.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2 style="text-align: center; color: #333; margin-top: 30px;">We include two additional measures in our regressions</h2>
    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
        <li>% of teachers in each school with &le; 3 years of teaching experience</li>
        <li>% of LEP students in each school</li>
    </ul>
</div>

